WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.410
While we wait to reunite with Dom, Letty,
and all the rest, we're passing the time by

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:07.600
rounding up all the spoilers and rumors we
can get our hands on.

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:09.100
Salud, mi familia.

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:14.700
After spinning its wheels for four commercially
successful but critically uneven films, the

00:00:14.709 --> 00:00:19.910
Fast and the Furious franchise really took
off with 2011's Fast Five, a slick, exuberant

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:24.570
heist action flick that bore little resemblance
to the smaller stakes street racing movies

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:25.500
that had come before it.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:29.640
One of its biggest upgrades came in the form
of Dwayne "The Rock" Johnson as Luke Hobbs,

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:34.620
a Diplomatic Security Service agent who served
as the film's intimidating antagonist.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.890
Hobbs would go on to follow in the footsteps
of former FBI agent Brian O'Conner, joining

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:43.880
up with the Fast Family rather than trying
to apprehend them for their big-hearted crimes.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.160
"Daddy's gotta go to work."

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:58.040
Jason Statham also joined the Fast and the
Furious series as rogue assassin Deckard Shaw,

00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.820
the family's deadliest antagonist.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:05.440
At the end of Fast &amp; Furious 6, he was revealed
to be the one who killed Han back in 2006's

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:07.240
The Fast and the Furious: Tokyo Drift.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:12.260
While many fans still haven't forgiven Shaw
for that, he also wound up joining forces

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:17.450
with Dom's crew, and was responsible for saving
Dom's infant son from Cipher in The Fate of

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:18.340
the Furious.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:23.350
But while Hobbs and Shaw proved to be so popular
that they got their own spinoff film, don't

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:26.180
expect to see them in the franchise's upcoming
ninth film.

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:31.450
In an interview with MTV News, Johnson confirmed
that he and Statham will not be appearing

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:35.120
there, although he left the door open for
an appearance in the already confirmed 10th

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:35.760
installment.

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:40.560
The absence of Luke Hobbs leaves some mighty
large shoes to fill, and who better to step

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:44.330
into them than that other wrestler-turned-actor,
John Cena?

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:49.090
While no character description has yet been
released, Universal has confirmed that Cena

00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:53.810
is indeed joining the Fast and the Furious
family, and his character is, to absolutely

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:56.340
no one's surprise, "a badass."

00:01:56.470 --> 00:02:00.780
Beyond that, who Cena will be playing is anyone's
guess, although it would be well within the

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.700
tradition of the franchise for him to make
his entrance as a villain.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:09.259
Johnson and Statham made the leap from antagonists
to heroes, as did Luke Evans' Fast &amp; Furious

00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:12.780
6 villain Owen Shaw, who helps save Dom's
son in Fate of the Furious.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:17.900
But Charlize Theron's baddie Cipher may also
be getting her own spin-off, hinting that

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:19.980
she too may wind up switching sides.

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:24.090
At this point, it would almost seem weird
for a Fast and the Furious movie to bring

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:26.720
on new big name and have them not play a villain.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.520
Chris Morgan has been writing the Fast and
the Furious scripts since Tokyo Drift, but

00:02:31.521 --> 00:02:36.490
with Morgan stepping away to pen Hobbs &amp; Shaw,
Fast 9 has tapped Daniel Casey to take over

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:38.140
writing duties for the ninth installment.

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:43.380
He's best known for 2018's Kin, but Casey
grabbed the studio's attention with his script

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:47.620
for The Heavy, a subversive superhero movie
that is currently in the works from producer

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:48.800
J.J. Abrams.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:52.760
It's fitting that Universal would look to
a superhero writer for the next Fast and the

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:57.210
Furious movie, considering the larger-than-life
direction the franchise has drifted in during

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.280
its latest installments.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:02.820
The stunts have been growing increasingly
more out-of-this-world for years.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:07.920
Fate of the Furious even includes jetpacks
like the one the Falcon wears in the Avengers

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:08.420
movies.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:13.100
Idris Elba's character and his cyborg-like
abilities might not just be a one off thing

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.140
"Look at me.

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:18.300
I'm Black Superman."

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:22.840
Perhaps Casey's hiring hints that superpowers
won't be limited to spinoffs, and that the

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:26.740
already-loose physics of the Fast and the
Furious series will get shrugged off entirely.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:31.459
While most of Dominic Toretto's crew joined
the franchise somewhere between the second

00:03:31.459 --> 00:03:35.760
and fifth films, Michelle Rodriguez has been
there from the very beginning, playing Dom's

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:38.620
girlfriend and eventual wife, Letty Ortiz.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:43.480
However, while Letty and Dom were closer than
ever at the end of The Fate of the Furious,

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:45.780
Rodriguez herself was a different story.

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:51.780
In an Instagram post in 2017, Rodriguez wrote
that she might consider walking if the Fast

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:54.140
franchise didn't give women a more prominent
role.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:58.740
Faced with a future without one of the family's
longest-tenured members, or perhaps simply

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:03.930
because the studio agreed with Rodriguez and
wanted to do right by its female fans, Universal

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:08.140
agreed to her stipulation that she would only
return if they hired a female writer for the

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:08.640
ninth movie.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:13.160
Although we still don't know who the woman
is who will be helping Daniel Casey pen the

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:17.519
script for Fast 9, we hope that Rodriguez
gets her wish and that the script does indeed

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.680
show the amazing women of the franchise some
love.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:24.600
During the filming of Furious 7, Paul Walker,
who had been playing Dom's best friend and

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:29.440
brother-in-law Brian O'Conner since the first
movie, was tragically killed in a car crash.

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:34.340
Instead of writing a similarly sad fate for
Brian, the ending of the film was rewritten

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:38.060
to bring closure to Brian's story, with him
riding off into the sunset.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:43.820
However, Vin Diesel announced in 2017 that
Jordana Brewster will be reprising her role

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:47.200
as Mia, Dom's sister and Brian's wife, for
Fast 9.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:51.940
Given how important it was to the entire cast
and crew of Furious 7 that Brian receive a

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:56.560
happy ending, it'll be interesting to see
how the series chooses to bring back Mia without

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:58.920
killing Brian off-screen or splitting them
up.

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:03.250
Hopefully, Brian's absence will be explained
by him staying home with the kids while Mia

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:05.360
goes off with her brother to help save the
world.

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:10.680
It seems like every fan-base in every franchise
wants the same actor to join up and “woah

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:13.640
- up” their perspective universe: Keanu
Reeves.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:17.840
Information has been murky about just how
big Reeves' role will be in the film.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:19.400
Could he be the villain?

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:24.360
And if he is the villain will he be the behind-the-scenes
type or out there John Wick-ing it up and

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.720
jumping from moving vehicles like a seasoned
vet?

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.400
Or will he even be in the movie at all?

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:33.860
Plenty of websites reported that Reeves would
appear in Hobbs and Shaw and - spoiler - he

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:34.360
didn’t.

00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:39.400
Just because people want Keanu in the movie,
it doesn’t mean it’ll happen - just ask

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:40.420
MCU fans.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:46.480
While the original The Fast and the Furious
was filmed entirely in and around Los Angeles,

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:48.640
the series has since shot all over the world.

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:51.520
"You're a long way from home.

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:56.560
This is Brazil!"

00:05:57.910 --> 00:06:01.940
In Fast 9, the series will be returning to
the U.K., with production confirmed to be

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:02.940
underway in London.

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:06.060
Other shooting locations include Los Angeles
and Hawaii.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:10.699
It's important to keep in mind that a shooting
location doesn't necessarily guarantee that

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:12.920
part of the film will be set in the same place.

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:19.260
For example, in Fast &amp; Furious 6, London stood
in for Moscow, and in The Fate of the Furious,

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:22.560
many of the "New York" scenes were actually
filmed in Cleveland.

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:27.020
Still, most of the time when the Furious films
travel abroad, it's because at least part

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:29.060
of the movie is set in the country they're
filming in.

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:33.590
So it's a safe bet that Dom and his crew will
be hopping across the pond for some of Fast

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:37.620
9, in addition to spending some time in at
least one more tropical locale.

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:42.410
When it comes to gender representation, the
Fast and Furious family has always been pretty

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:43.920
heavy on the dude side of things.

00:06:44.600 --> 00:06:48.520
Fortunately, it seems as though Fast 9 may
be taking some steps to correct that.

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:52.900
Michelle Rodriguez, Jordana Brewster, and
Nathalie Emmanuel are already set to reprise

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:58.400
their roles as Letty, Mia, and Ramsey, respectively,
along with the as-yet unannounced female writer

00:06:58.400 --> 00:06:59.660
joining the creative team.

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:04.740
In addition to these three established women
of the Fast and the Furious world, Chris Bridges,

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:10.940
aka Ludacris, who has played Tej Parker in
the series since 2 Fast 2 Furious in 2003,

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:16.280
took to his Instagram in early 2019 to tease
an intriguing possible addition to the cast.

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:22.720
He posted a photo captioned "masterminding"
of himself, his F&amp;F cast-mate Vin Diesel,

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:27.140
and an actress moviegoers might recognize
from John Wick: Chapter 2: Ruby Rose.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:31.600
Of course, a single Instagram post doesn't
necessarily mean that Rose is joining the

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:32.480
Furious family.

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:37.420
Even Luda's return for Fast 9 hasn't been
confirmed yet, although it seems pretty likely

00:07:37.430 --> 00:07:41.190
that he'll be back in action, even if the
photo was taken just during a chill hangout

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:41.760
among pals.

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:46.580
It's worth noting, however, that Diesel is
one of the masterminds of the franchise both

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:50.060
onscreen as Dom and behind the scenes as producer.

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:54.140
Considering that Rose previously appeared
alongside Diesel in Triple X: The Return of

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:58.550
Xander Cage and that she's set to find new
fame as the defender of Gotham City in the

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:03.520
CW's upcoming Batwoman series, Rose seems
more than equipped to join this team of masterminds.

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:08.500
In the same Facebook Live video in which Vin
Diesel announced Jordana Brewster's return

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:12.910
to the Fast and the Furious family, he also
delightedly revealed that after a few years'

00:08:12.910 --> 00:08:17.900
absence and a trip on board the starship Enterprise,
director Justin Lin would be helming both

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:19.960
the ninth and tenth movies in the series.

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:24.820
Lin joined the Fast and the Furious series
in 2006, taking the reins on The Fast and

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:30.480
the Furious: Tokyo Drift and staying with
the films through 2013's Fast &amp; Furious 6.

00:08:31.009 --> 00:08:35.099
Other directors took over after that, with
James Wan coming aboard for Furious 7 and

00:08:35.099 --> 00:08:39.310
F. Gary Gray stepping in for The Fate of the
Furious, but now Lin is back for what are

00:08:39.310 --> 00:08:42.100
expected to be the final two installments
in the saga.

00:08:42.409 --> 00:08:46.120
Diesel said prior to the release of The Fate
of the Furious that the reason he decided

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:50.360
to continue the franchise following Paul Walker's
death while filming the seventh movie was

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:52.420
because Walker, quote, "promised eight."

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:56.620
He went on to explain that The Fate of the
Furious would kick off a new trilogy that

00:08:56.620 --> 00:08:57.740
would change the series.

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:03.140
Considering that the plot of Fate involved
literal nuclear warheads, it's safe to say

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:03.720
they delivered.

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:08.140
Now that Lin, who was responsible for taking
the series to new extremes, is returning to

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:11.960
shepherd the series through its final films,
things only seem like they're going to get

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:12.460
bigger.

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:16.879
Nathalie Emmanuel first joined the Fast and
the Furious crew as the mysterious master

00:09:16.879 --> 00:09:21.929
hacker Ramsey in Furious 7, after she was
kidnapped for inventing a hacking device called

00:09:21.929 --> 00:09:22.760
the God's Eye.

00:09:23.189 --> 00:09:27.160
Needless to say, she was subsequently rescued
by Dominic Toretto and the Family, and the

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:32.149
next time we saw her in Fate of the Furious,
she was an indispensable member of the team.

00:09:32.149 --> 00:09:35.981
and now that we know she's returning for Fast
9, we can only hope that Ramsey will be a

00:09:35.981 --> 00:09:38.540
member of the Fast family all the way until
the end of the road.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:43.550
We know Emmanuel is on her way back thanks
to a tweet she made back in June, but that

00:09:43.550 --> 00:09:45.840
wasn't the only part of it that got fans excited.

00:09:46.260 --> 00:09:50.110
In addition to her announcement, she also
included a row of emojis that look a whole

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:53.780
lot like the rest of the core cast, including
Tyrese Gibson and Ludacris.

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:58.740
Their characters, Roman and Tej, have long
been assumed to be returning for Fast 9, but

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:00.420
hadn't been officially confirmed.

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:05.420
Emojis may not be the most official means
of confirmation, but it's looking increasingly

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:10.300
likely that the whole Fast family, minus their
spin-off pals in Hobbs &amp; Shaw, will be joining

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:12.120
forces yet again for Fast 9.

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:15.080
Maybe they can finally figure out what her
full name is!

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:17.560
"Let me ask you one question."

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:18.800
"You can ask me anything."

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:20.480
"Anything?"

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:21.940
"What's my last name?"

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:26.300
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:30.440
Plus, even more Looper videos about The Fast
and the Furious franchise are coming soon.

00:10:30.860 --> 00:10:34.520
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

